      "writtenOn": "2013-07-26T17:57:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree your change fixes ver.2, but it breaks ver.3 as currently implemented in the kernel driver.\n\n1) proto3 max in/out size varies based on EC buffer sizes.  Fetchable via EC_CMD_GET_PROTOCOL_INFO.\n\n2) U-boot / coreboot / kernel also allocate buffers based on some size calculations or magic numbers.  I don\u0027t know how they do this.  It should really be based on the result of EC_CMD_GET_PROTOCOL_INFO for ver.3, and hard-coded constants in ec_commands.h for ver.2, but I believe it just uses the ver.2 limits - except that ver.3 has more overhead (8 bytes instead of 5).\n\n3) There isn\u0027t (yet) an IOCTL for ectool/flashrom to find these limits.  Hence the magic numbers.\n\nIt\u0027s safe to increase the maximum input size, because even if you set that to 100MB the EC will still be bound by its limits.  That is, increasing the input size limit won\u0027t change what data you actually receive.\n\nBut it\u0027s not safe to increase the maximum output size, because you can create a packet which is too big for either the kernel driver or the EC.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAcX//uuo\u003d",
      "revId": "4001d96f565b9bf88bf5882f09da373b07b053eb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
